<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaspar Pacheco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaspar Pacheco was a Spanish conquistador in the conquest of Yucatán. In 1544, serving under the Montejos, he and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melchor-pacheco">Melchor Pacheco</a> led the campaign that conquered Uaymil, Chetumal and neighbouring Maya provinces in the south-east of the peninsula. Their campaign was notorious even among contemporaries for its cruelty, including mutilations and killings of captives, and it left the region largely depopulated.</p></div>
